  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SHE CRAFT WOMEN GROUP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &#x2018;&#x2019;Crafting skills with Confidence&#x2019;&#x2019; Seeks to further empower women war victims through enhancing their skills in tailoring  and craft making businesses as a cope up strategy that in the long run aid a reduction to their economic hardships, physical insecurity and increase women&#x2019;s access to productive resources such as land and other valuable assets. This project will leverage on skilling women war victims from northern Uganda who emerged as survivors of war,  fighting in frontlines as a result of abduction by the LRA, suffering multiple abuses especially sexual violence and forced marriages, are faced with realities of difficulties in providing for children born of war, their conditions and  statelessness including their education. They are suffering from multiple discriminations based on being survivors of war, unwanted pregnancies, STIs, HIV because of gang rape, restricted mobility due to socialnorms, job insecurity, discriminatory legal and social environment, harmful social and gender norms, and economic inequality.   The18 months project will empower the women war victims and survivors through capacity enhancement in constructing and tailoring for improved quality of life, wellbeing of children and war affected communities
The project envisions these women stepping out/up their socially ascribed roles to respond to crisis and use their skills, information accessed and exposure to challenge the long standing stereotypes as voiceless by participating in decision making at both household and community level.</narrative>
  </description>
